If the first of four browser render-worker attempts fails, messages from the surviving workers are associated with the wrong slots. The app reports only two ready workers despite three actual ready replies, and render jobs remain pending even after worker job replies arrive.

## Environment

- Current main `7aab3fd97fed00ffcebdd3cca7fede12f7672194`, fresh release web build; Rust 1.95.0, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.
- Local host with COOP/COEP; `?store=memory&workers=4`.
- macOS 26.5.2 arm64, Apple M1; isolated headless Chrome 154.0.8037.93, Firefox 155.0 and Playwright WebKit 26.6 (not Safari).

## Reproduction

Install this before application scripts run, for example with Playwright `browserContext.addInitScript`:

```js
const OriginalWorker = Worker;
let attempted = 0;
window.workerReplies = [];
window.Worker = class extends OriginalWorker {
  constructor(url, options) {
    const index = attempted++;
    if (index === 0) {
      throw new DOMException('Injected first worker failure', 'SecurityError');
    }
    super(url, options);
    this.addEventListener('message', event => {
      workerReplies.push({ index, ready: event.data?.ready, id: event.data?.id });
    });
  }
};
```

1. Start LightCraft with `?store=memory&workers=4`.
2. Import a generated 128×128 white PNG with a 32×32 red upper-left corner.
3. Export PNG, set exposure to −1 EV and export again, then Undo and export again. Inspect the actual downloads independently.
