AFAIK there is no public repository nor common format for lens profiles, but I believe there are many photo geeks who will happily suggest a proper format and contribute measurements for their lenses given opportunity.

Ideally we'd need for every lens a barrel distortion, CA, and vignetting values/curves per focal range and f-stop. Static values are fine, but curves would be perfect (for varied zoom and de-clicked iris).

As for generation of these files, this could be implemented as part of LightcraftUI. 
For example:
* User takes a photo of measurement chart at various focal ranges and f-stops;
* Adjusts lens corrections for every photo for best results;
* Select edited photos and pick "Generate lens-correction values". This opens dialog. This dialog pulls range and f-stop from EXIF;
* User do final adjustments, tune the curves or add missing values;
* Click [save] to save local version or [export] to make a json file to post a MR in this repo.

